; Frame routine of the title and controls menus
;
; Called by the interrupt handler through the vector at $8504. The start of the game #R$85FC installs it before the
; title is drawn and replaces it with #R$85E2 when the game starts. Each frame it runs the sound effects (#R$871A),
; reads the keyboard into #R$A2D3 (#R$A240), finds the first key held (#R$A29C) and stores its half-row index and mask
; in $8502/$8503 (the mask in $8502, the row in $8503; read by #R$A3B9), then finishes with #R$A304 which sets the key
; code #R$A2D2.
; .
; Hardware: beeper (through #R$871A) and keyboard ports (through #R$A240).
;
; O:A Key code of the key held, 0 for none
@label=MenuFrame
c$A43D CALL $871A    ;
 $A440 CALL $A240    ;
 $A443 CALL $A29C    ;
 $A446 LD ($8502),BC ; $8502 = mask of the key found, $8503 = its half-row index
 $A44A JP $A304      ; tail call: the key code goes to #R$A2D2
